  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "On the 1969 Apollo 11 Moon landing, Buzz Aldrin was supposedly under orders that if Neil Armstrong went out first and anything happened to him, Aldrin \"was not supposed to play the hero\", meaning he was not to try to rescue him. The UFO documentary maker James Fox tells Michels this, passing on what he was told, and names a woman called Fay Ann Potter among his sources. If true, it would mean NASA had planned coldly for losing a man on the Moon."
